A||N||3||Ben84||Speaker Installation||||6||
Z||000000||Ben84||08-14-2001||09:28 AM||||For 3.5 speaker installation, what Ohm should the speakers be, to prevent damage to head unit... The 3.5 will be installed parallel due to lack of a harness (previous owner).... I have some polk 4 ohm speakers... I afraid of damage to the aftermarket CD player....||||reg||6
Z||000001||LarryB||08-14-2001||09:45 AM||||It depends on what you're using for a head unit.  If the amp is 2 ohm stable (Delco units aren't) you can get away with another speaker rated at 4 ohm impedance.   Most of the good aftermarket units are rated as being 2 ohm stable.<P>If you're wiring the speakers in parallel, the equivalent impedance the amp will see on that channel can be expressed as:<P>             (x*y)/(x+y)<P>where x = impedance of speaker #1<BR>and   y = impedance of speaker #2<P>whereas if you wire them in series the formula becomes simply:<P>              (x+y)<P>If you wire 2 speakers in parallel with different rated impedances you can also expect different volume levels out of each.<BR>Depending on what you're doing, that may or not be important. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||08-14-2001||11:00 AM||||AHHH!!!! keep the speakers in the seats on different channels! thats whats cool about them is they are in stereo, so when songs have like a plane fly by or something it sounds great. run new wires to the front, not hard will only take another 30 minutes<P>kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieronv||08-14-2001||12:12 PM||||I agree with the previous post. If you need to know if your after market cd head is stable to 2 ohms go to the makers web site and look in the technical support section or call them. I added Blaupunkt 3.5 in my seats a couple of months ago and wired the speakers in series to get the speakers to 8 ohms. My car did not come with the factory wiring so I had to add the wiring. I took out the center console to ease the install. It took me about a hour to complete the wiring and re-install the console well worth the effort and to keep the head rest speaker in stereo. I later added another amplifer (2 ohm stable) and re wired the speakers to parallel. so say the least they sound great and add a lot of depth to my system. I plan in the future to upgrade my system to include a car theatre and use these as rear channel speakers. Check out this thread for pictures of the install of my system. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009358.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009358.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||4
